  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Acelerando la accion regional a favor de los Derechos Humanos, Sexuales y Reproductivos y la No Violencia hacia las Mujeres con VIH - Americas - Multicountry Americas ICW (01-Jan-2016-31-Dec-2018)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry Americas ICW, HIV, Humanist Institute for Co-operation with Developing Countries (Hivos) (HIVOS -  HubLA)This program has the following goals: Empower women living with HIV in Latin America for them to demand their right to access a comprehensive HIV response that addressses their needs, with the aim to create an enabling environment to live without violence and improve their quality of life. The objectives of this program are: Capacity building for WLHIV leaders in terms of their knowledge, skills and abilities related to human rights and violence against WLHIV, including international goals and mechanisms, awareness-raising processes on human rights, health and sexual and reproductive rights, access to justice and a community approach..  Guarantee the effective participation of WLHIV in Latin America in regional and subregional decision-making spaces to raise awareness about HIV and its links to gender inequality and violence against women and to include these in policies and programs..  Strategically document, disseminate and use key information and good practices on the link between HIV in women, health, sexual and reproductive rights and violence against WLHIV..  Strengthen ICW Latina&apos;s regional community system to help make its actions more sustainable.</narrative>
  </description>
